it":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer is made in promoting a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to the client, including promotional linkage to a type such as funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The product or product type to which this benefit's promotion is connected falls within the circular's SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","name":"promotion_concerns_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection)"},"local_id":"reading_1","questions":["Does paragraph 3.11 confirm the general product scope of this restatement despite the circular's fund-specific subject?"],"statement":"Selected control: general-product gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific investment product or a particular product type is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. This includes promotional linkage to a fund type or fund house. The restriction does not depend on the arrangement being a structured product or on demonstrated distraction.","subject":"Whether an identified offer is caught by the selected paragraph-10 gift restriction"},{"assumptions":["Each evaluation concerns one identified benefit offer to one client; a campaign requires assessment of every relevant offer.","The actor must be a distributor as defined in u1; the Code's title alone does not expand this actor definition.","The circular's SFC-authorised-fund context limits this selected application of the general wording quoted in u14.","Product-type linkage in the promotion is sufficient; proof of actual distraction is not an additional condition.","Unknown classification or scope facts remain unknown."],"citations":[{"quote":"This circular summarises the Securities and Futures Commission’s (SFC) recent observations of licensed corporations’ practices in offering and promoting SFC-authorised funds.","unit_id":"u1"},{"quote":"in offering such returns or other incentives in promoting SFC-authorised funds","unit_id":"u13"},{"quote":"distributors should not offer any gifts (other than a discount of fees or charges) in promoting a specific investment product or a particular type of investment product to a client.","unit_id":"u14"},{"quote":"when offering or promoting funds, distributors should not offer additional returns","unit_id":"u15"}],"distinction":"The same distributor's gift promoting only a different investment product is outside this selected application, while gifts connected to SFC-authorised funds remain covered. Outside scope does not mean permitted under the full Code. The strongest uncertainty is that u14 itself states no express SFC-authorised-fund limitation.","family":"scope","formalization":{"facts":[{"meaning":"The actor is an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds within the distributor description in u1.","name":"is_distributor","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u29"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit is offered to a client; actual acceptance or delivery is unnecessary for this offer fact.","name":"benefit_offered_to_client","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit qualifies as a gift, assessed before applying the express discount exception; an additional return or incentive is not automatically classified as a gift.","name":"benefit_is_gift","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u13","u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The identified benefit itself qualifies as a discount of fees or charges within u14's exception; merely including a discount elsewhere in a package is insufficient to establish this fact.","name":"benefit_is_fee_discount","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The offer is made in promoting a specific investment product or particular investment-product type to the client, including promotional linkage to a type such as funds from certain fund houses.","name":"has_product_promotion_connection","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u14"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"},{"meaning":"The product or product type to which this benefit's promotion is connected falls within the circular's SFC-authorised-fund subject matter.","name":"promotion_concerns_authorised_funds","requires_judgment":true,"source_unit_ids":["u1","u13","u15"],"type":"bool","unit":"truth value"}],"result":"(and benefit_is_gift (not benefit_is_fee_discount))","result_type":"bool","scope":"(and is_distributor benefit_offered_to_client has_product_promotion_connection promotion_concerns_authorised_funds)"},"local_id":"reading_2","questions":["Is the fund-specific context a limit on this circular's selected application, or merely the occasion for restating a broader control?"],"statement":"Selected control: fund-context gift-offer restriction. For an intermediary distributing SFC-authorised funds, an identified benefit offered to a client in promoting a specific SFC-authorised fund or a particular type of such funds is caught by the 'should not offer' restriction if it is a gift and is not a qualifying fee-or-charge discount. Product-type linkage includes relevant funds offered by certain fund houses. Structured-product status and actual distraction are not additional conditions.","subject":"Whether an identified offer is caught by the selected paragraph-10 gift restriction"}]}},"run_id":"run.d6106e5450c749a58852e36e6f81a6e0"}